     <rdf:li
      photoshop:LayerName="  In applications involving the transfer through the hose of ex"
      photoshop:LayerText="  In applications involving the transfer through the hose of expensive or dangerous fluids or gases, the hoses and connections must be pressure tested in site before being put in to service. This should be done with some harmless media to 1Â½ times the maximum working pressure of the hose assembly."/>
     <rdf:li
      photoshop:LayerName="Connecting Assemblies for Use in Applications "
      photoshop:LayerText="Connecting Assemblies for Use in Applications "/>
     <rdf:li
      photoshop:LayerName=" When being connected for use in applications, the end fittings"
      photoshop:LayerText=" When being connected for use in applications, the end fittings on hose assemblies must be connected to correct mating parts in the correct way, using the correct tools, spanners, clamps, nuts and bolts etc. The connections must be sufficiently tightened to ensur that the joint is leak free but not be over tightened as this can damage the sealing surfaces."/>
     <rdf:li
      photoshop:LayerName="The performance testing results stated in the above table have "
      photoshop:LayerText="The performance testing results stated in the above table have been carried out at ambient temperature, in a controlled laboratory environment, using water as the media. We recommend that the customer carries out stringent application performance testing on the hose, using the actual working conditions over a set period of time to validate the hose.  * Tolerance Â± 0,6 mm, wall thickness of PTFE liner may vary due to nature of liner productions ** Burst pressure values apply to hose only"/>
     <rdf:li
      photoshop:LayerName="Fluid applications Fuel, Oil, Water, Methanol &amp; Pneumatics  Ara"
      photoshop:LayerText="Fluid applications Fuel, Oil, Water, Methanol &amp; Pneumatics  Aramid Fibre Braid The aramid fibre is Tecnora, a higher specification fibre than Kevlar, with excellent temperature, tensile and abrasion resistant properties. For applications requiring minimum weight for maximum pressure reinforcement.  Reduced diffusion rates S-Series Hose is much more resistant to diffusion of liquids or gases than other PTFE hose products, due to its highly compressed, non-p rous PTFE matrix. S-Series Hose has been successfully tested to SAE J1737 for resistance to automotive fuel diffusion.  Antistatic PTFE Linings When electrically resistive fluids like solvents and fuels, or multiphase mixtures are passed through natural PTFE hose at high flow rates, a static charge build up occurs on the inner wall of the PTFE liner. This can discharge to the nearest conductor that creates a pin-hole in the PTFE liner resulting in a leak-path. Antistatic PTFE includes a small quantity of a special high purity carbon black, which ensures safe static charge dissipation in accordance with International Standards."/>
     <rdf:li
      photoshop:LayerName="Compatible fittings S-Series S7 crimp fittings  Excellent flow "
      photoshop:LayerText="Compatible fittings S-Series S7 crimp fittings  Excellent flow rates Compared with conventional convoluted hose designs, S-Series Hose has excellent flow rates due to the smooth bore, which prevents the turbulent fluid flow which occurs in convoluted hose products.  Non-stick internal surface S-Series Hose has a smooth bore, non-stick liner which is effectively self-cleaning, and which resists material build-up inside the hose which may cause bore constriction.  Temperatures and pressures The MWP listed above should be reduced by 1% for each 1 Â°C above 130 Â°C up to a maximum of 180 Â°C. MWP listed are calculated on the basis of a 3:1 safety factor relative to the burst pressure, so burst pressure = 3 x MWP. If MWP is required based on a 4:1 safety factor (e.g. EN 16643 requirement), multiply the listed value by 0.75. Resistant to temperatures from -40Â°C to 180Â°C  "/>
